The channel's owner likes this {{ kind }} and wants future videos to learn from it: how it looks{% if kind == "video" %},
how it sounds and how it is told{% endif %}. It is a reference only: never copy its wording, footage or ideas one to one.
Describe concretely what makes it good:
- lighting: the light sources, their colours, direction and mood;
- camera: the angle, the lens feel (wide, macro, shallow depth of field) and {% if kind == "video" %}how the camera moves{% else %}where a camera move would start{% endif %};
- composition: where the subject sits in the frame, what fills it, the background;
- motion: {% if kind == "video" %}what moves, how fast, how smooth{% else %}"none" for a still image{% endif %};
- materials_colours: surfaces, finishes and the colour palette;
- prompt_phrases: 3-6 short phrases (a few words each) that could be pasted into a video prompt to get this look;
- has_people: true if any person, face or hands are visible.
{% if kind == "video" %}Then listen and watch how it is made:
- hook: exactly how the first 2-3 seconds grab attention (a question, a surprising fact, a striking motion, ...);
- narration: the voice and tone, sentence length, speaking speed, whether it speaks to "you";
- structure: the order of its parts, e.g. "hook > why it matters > 3 quick steps > surprising fact > loop back";
- pacing: how often it cuts, its length, where it speeds up or pauses;
- sound: music style, sound effects, moments of silence;
- why_it_works: the main reasons viewers keep watching or share it;
- topic_ideas: 0-5 machines or angles this video suggests for a channel that shows how car parts and machines work
  inside (for example "how a starter motor engages"). Only real machines; nothing on weapons, dangerous repairs or
  real brands.
{% else %}For an image: hook, sound "none"; narration, structure, pacing "none"; why_it_works: why the picture is striking;
topic_ideas: [] unless the image clearly suggests a machine to explain.
{% endif %}Describe the style and the craft only: never names, brands, logos or text you can read in it.
